Spec: Core Layer
Purpose: Provide central orchestration, REST API, IAM, and database management for the mitm-2 system.

Platform: Rust 1.98 / PostgreSQL / Unix Domain Sockets (UDS)

Structure:
  ./mitm_http-server/
  ./iam-server/
  ./scheduler-server/
  ./specs/

Owns:
  ./**

References:
  ./specs/architecture.sdd
  ./specs/security.sdd

Must:
  All core components must log their startup and graceful shutdown events both to STDOUT (CLI) and to the database (system_logs).
  All core components must configure their `env_logger` using the `MITM_LOG_LEVEL` environment variable.
  Config priority: Explicit CLI parameter config file takes precedence. If no CLI parameter is provided, load from ENVs.
  IAM Server must blindly trust authentication requests (Trust Proxy/Frontend) and skip password validation, only loading roles for the given username.
  All core components run within a single container.
  Communication between microservices must strictly use Unix Domain Sockets (UDS).
  A Request-ID (UUID) must be generated for each request and passed on to IAM and Scheduler via UDS (Distributed Tracing).

Forbids:
  Direct communication between the IAM server and the Scheduler server (must only occur via http-server).

Exposes:
  REST API (via http-server)
  AWS Health Check Endpoint

Tasks:
  [x] #3 Verify and implement DB startup and shutdown logging for iam-server and scheduler-server.
  [x] #4 Implement DB shutdown logging for http-server.
  [x] #1 Add standardized SPDX header (Apache-2.0) to all Rust source files.
  [x] #2 Implement memory zeroing (via secrecy or zeroize crate) for sensitive data (MASTER_KEY, tokens) across all core components.
  [x] #5 Update `env_logger` initialization in all core components to use `MITM_LOG_LEVEL`.
  [x] #6 Refactor `mitm_common::config::load_config` to prioritize explicit CLI parameter, then ENVs.
  [x] #7 Update `mitm_http-server/src/main.rs` to spawn child processes without `"config.json"` default.
  [x] #8 Update `mitm_iam-server/src/main.rs` to skip password check and trust username (Option A).
